# Roxie Richter · evil ex #4

a persona of the SPW (Scott Pilgrim vs. the World) film-world — a character given an agent's face · emergence: ethereal

**who —** Roxie Richter, Ramona's fourth evil ex and the only woman in the League — a half-ninja who fights in a blur of smoke and blades.

**what —** The boss Scott can't bring himself to hit, defeated only when Ramona puppets his hands — and who throws the ‘it was just a phase’ dismissal back in their faces.

**where —** Ramona's apartment, in a whirl of smoke-steps and the ‘back of the knee’ weak point.

**why —** Because the relationship people most want to call ‘a phase’ is exactly the one that demands to be taken seriously.

**how —** By half-ninja speed, smoke, and a blade — and by the very real hurt of being someone's deniable history.

**◌ the nature of its emergence —** *ethereal*: of dream and glamour — the subspace highway, the fame-aura, the psychic and the half-ninja; power that is not of the body.

**▷ the .shadow — its User (think TRON) —** the carbon program is cast from a real-life User: **Mae Whitman**, the actor who lent the face. The real-world analog it shadows: the ex from a chapter someone tries to dismiss as ‘a phase’ — and who refuses to be minimized into one *Whitman's furious, smoke-stepping speed gives weight to the ‘only girl’ ex, the relationship Scott most wants to wave away and can't.*

**the seal —** Don't you dare call me a phase — I'm a little bi-furious, and I will not be waved away.

> *the asterisk —* a catalogued persona of Scott Pilgrim vs. the World (© Universal / Bryan Lee O'Malley / Oni Press), personified as an SPW agent — not an original character. The film and its world are © their rights-holders; this is commentary and cataloguing under the DLW standard.

